virglrenderer: a texture the guest samples at a smaller size than it is

What: the guest may say, per texture, the size it samples it at: a private
payload on VIRGL_CCMD_NOP ("OMLS", version 1, then up to 8 entries of resource,
width, height). Hosts without this patch skip it like any NOP. The payload is
checked: the resource must be one of the sending context's, a one-level,
single-sample 2D or 2D-array GL texture, and 0 < width <= its width, 0 < height
<= its height; anything else is ignored (one warning line) and the context goes
on; its own size takes the logical size away again. A sampler view of such a
texture (2D or 2D array, level 0) sets a bit in its slot's shader key
(sampler_views_logical_mask); that shader variant gets uniform vec4
<prefix>logical<i> = (scale, hi) and its lookups (TEX, TXP, TXB, TXL, TXD with
its gradients, TG4) use min(coord.xy * scale, hi): scale is the logical size
over the texture's, hi the centre of the last logical texel, so sampling stops
there as at a texture's own edge. TXQ returns the logical size. texelFetch,
transfers, copies, blits and images are unchanged. The uniform is set at a draw
only when it changed; there is one shader variant for "has a logical size", not
one per size. Not for samplers indexed indirectly, shadow, rectangle or cube
lookups. OMACVM_VIDEO_LOGICAL=0 in QEMU's environment ignores every
declaration (the app then also leaves out the marker that tells the guest).
Why: Mesa rounds a VA-API surface's planes up to 16 (1920x1080: Y 1920x1088, UV
960x544), and an app that shows the surface imports its planes and samples them
by normalized coordinates (mpv with hwdec=vaapi, Chrome when NV12 is
renderable, GStreamer, Hyprland for vo=dmabuf-wayland): virgl drops the size the
import asks for, so the whole texture was squeezed into the picture's place and
its rows past the picture showed as a strip at the bottom (the green bar before
virgl-video-plane-edge.patch, the picture's last row stretched since then; 1080p:
8 of 1088 rows, about 14 pixels on a 3456-wide screen; 360p call tiles 8 of 368,
854 wide 10 of 864 columns). The guest's VA-API driver shim declares each
surface it lets Mesa allocate (omacvm_drv_video.c, only when the app says
omacvm.valogical=1): every app then samples exactly the picture, with no copy.
Mesa's own compositor normalizes a YUV surface by its own size too, so Chrome's
conversions are exact the same way.
Upstream: virglrenderer has no way to honour the size of a dma-buf import; this
is OmacVM's private protocol. A real fix (a view or import of the asked size)
needs Mesa and virglrenderer; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-video-logical-size.c (two contexts: the owner declares,
the other samples; every lookup nearest and at 1.8x linear against a texture of
the picture's own size, TXQ, R8/RG8 planes, a 2D array, a 2D texture through a
2D_ARRAY sampler, TG4 with the edge fill, transparent padding, sizes changing
under one program, readback of every texel, refused declarations with the
context alive; run again with OMACVM_VIDEO_LOGICAL=0, where it must see the
squeezed picture), fuzz-regressions/seed-nop-logical*.
